From: "vlad.maglasu" <vlad.maglasu@vampirebyte.ro>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:36:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(iso15118): poll the PollManager's eventfd from
 construction, close it on destruction

PollManager built its poll set only in register_fd() and unregister_fd(). Since
the TbdController binds the network interface in tick(), after its first
poll(), that poll() got an empty set: pollfds.data() is NULL with nfds 0.
Linux waits for the timeout, but abort() cannot wake it because the eventfd
is not in the set; ESP-IDF's poll() rejects fds == NULL with ENOENT, so the
loop failed before the interface was ever bound.

The constructor now builds the poll set with the eventfd. The destructor closes
the eventfd, which leaked with every PollManager.

Signed-off-by: vlad.maglasu <vlad.maglasu@vampirebyte.ro>

diff --git a/iso15118/include/iso15118/io/poll_manager.hpp b/iso15118/include/iso15118/io/poll_manager.hpp
index 7aaa54e..e296007 100644
--- a/iso15118/include/iso15118/io/poll_manager.hpp
+++ b/iso15118/include/iso15118/io/poll_manager.hpp
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ struct PollSet {
 class PollManager {
 public:
     PollManager();
+    ~PollManager();
 
     void register_fd(int fd, PollCallback& poll_callback);
     void unregister_fd(int fd);
diff --git a/iso15118/src/iso15118/io/poll_manager.cpp b/iso15118/src/iso15118/io/poll_manager.cpp
index 0072e65..2fee4b2 100644
--- a/iso15118/src/iso15118/io/poll_manager.cpp
+++ b/iso15118/src/iso15118/io/poll_manager.cpp
@@ -37,6 +37,13 @@ PollManager::PollManager() {
     if (event_fd == -1) {
         log_and_throw("Failed to create eventfd");
     }
+    // Polled from the start: abort() must wake a poll() before the first register_fd(), and poll() must not be
+    // handed an empty set (fds == NULL, which some platforms reject).
+    poll_set = create_poll_set(registered_fds, event_fd);
+}
+
+PollManager::~PollManager() {
+    close(event_fd);
 }
 
 void PollManager::register_fd(int fd, PollCallback& poll_callback) {
